/code-review high — loop R1, round 2 — range 554a7d40..2bfde1db (branch 2026-10-08-execute-renders-served-at-a-url)

I reviewed 554a7d40..2bfde1db, leaving out `docs/plans/`. I found 10 issues and haven't run anything to confirm them. Three are correctness bugs:

1. In `renders.mjs`, when a screen's route moves and the image is re-rendered, the old image is left on disk. The render server can then show it as a different screen's render.
2. The `RENDER:` line has no project field. When the execute step runs the copy once per project, the orchestrator can't split the lines, so a screen code shared by two projects puts one project's image in the other's tree.
3. `renders.mjs` exits 0 and reports `COPIED: n` even when writing `renders.json` and `routes.json` fails. The execute step only treats a non-zero exit as a gap, so that failure is never reported.

I didn't report missing user-manual or readme updates: the plan leaves those to its later docs unit (U5).

